  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 246 PM MDT Sun Sep 13 2026\n\nWinds remain the main story of the day as gusts continue to \nincrease especially across the northern half of the Snake River \nPlain this afternoon. Wind Advisory remains in effect for Zones \n52 and 67 (Arco/Mud Lake and Beaverhead/Lemhi regions) until \nearly evening, with winds diminishing below 30 mph during the \nevening but remaining breezy overnight. Weak feature rotating \naround the center of low to the west times out to pass through \nEast Idaho this evening into the overnight. CAMs have picked up \non potential for light showers across the eastern highlands late\nthis evening, shifting east out of the state by sunrise. \nDaytime temps remain cool today compared to previous days, but \ndeepest cooling arrives Monday with temperatures dropping into \nthe mid to upper 60s for most. \n\nEast Idaho remains under the influence of trough to the west for\nmuch of the week. Gradual warming trend will be in place with\ndry conditions into mid week. By Thursday, next low feature\nshifts toward the region, and models are depicting trajectory\nsimilar to current low. East Idaho could see precipitation\ndevelop for Thursday and Friday, along with another round of\nbreezy winds.",
